"Zhengxiu Sun","LIN Yong’ao","Jinling Liu","Xingyu Xiong","Pinghao Li","Tianxi Ma","周明凯","Xiaoqin Guo","Chuyu Hang","Mingyuan Wang","Yuan Han","Hongxing Zhang","Song Zhang","He Liu","Jun‐Li Cao"],"published":"2026-10-06","year":2026,"month":10,"pdf_url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-77236-2","has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":["HealthMon"],"venue":"Nature Communications","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0},{"id":"openalex:W7220690846","title":"A generative diffusion framework for physically consistent 3D turbulence","authors":["Tianyi Li","Michele Buzzicotti","Fabio Bonaccorso","Luca Biferale"],"published":"2026-10-06","year":2026,"month":10,"pdf_url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-78265-7","has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":["DiffusionWM","PINN","FluidSim","HealthMon"],"_topics":["3d turbulence modeling","physical constraints satisfaction"],"venue":"Nature Communications","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0,"summary_zh":"提出物理约束扩散模型，直接将先验约束纳入生成动力学。以旋转湍流为例，展示其稳定且统计上忠实于惯性范围的3D湍流合成。","summary_en":"Proposed a physics-constrained diffusion model where some a priori constraints can be directly incorporated into the generative dynamics. Demonstrated its stable and statistically faithful synthesis of three-dimensional turbulence in the inertial range using rotating turbulence as an example.","insights":["创新点：物理约束扩散模型，提高湍流合成质量","方法亮点：直接将先验约束纳入生成动力学","关键发现：旋转湍流合成稳定且忠实"],"insights_en":["Novelty: Physics-constrained diffusion model, improves quality of turbulence synthesis","Method highlight: Directly incorporates a priori constraints into generative dynamics","Key finding: Rotating turbulence synthesis is stable and statistically faithful"],"abstract":"Abstract Synthesizing fully developed three-dimensional turbulence remains a long-standing problem in fluid mechanics and an open challenge for generative modeling. This difficulty arises from extreme dimensionality, multiscale fluctuations, strong intermittency, and the need to satisfy exact physical constraints, including incompressibility and prescribed mass and momentum fluxes under given boundary conditions. We propose a physics-constrained diffusion model in which some a priori constraints can be incorporated directly into the generative dynamics. Using rotating turbulence as a paradigmatic system with key geophysical applications, we assess the proposed framework. Here, we show that it enables stable and statistically faithful single-time synthesis of inertial-range three-dimensional turbulent velocity fields, accurately reproducing anisotropic energy spectra, intermittent statistics, and physical constraints, whereas standard denoising diffusion probabilistic models exhibit multiscale statistical deviations, violations of physical consistency, and substantially slower training convergence, thereby pointing to broader implications for generative modeling of high-dimensional, physically constrained complex systems."},{"id":"openalex:W7220692830","title":"Neonatal overfeeding accelerates age-related sarcopenia and metabolic disorders through lifelong gut mucosa and microbiota programming in mice","authors":["Yeyu Song","Jingyi Xu","Jingjie Zhao","Rong Yang","马援第","Yi-Ming Hou","Yutang Cao","Jiaqi Li","Shuwu Yu","XinYu Liang","Yongxin Zhang","Kanglong Wang","Lijuan An","Yameng Liu","Zhuo‐Xian Meng","Jian-Gao Fan","Cen Xie"],"published":"2026-10-07","year":2026,"month":10,"pdf_url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-78216-2","has_code":false,"type":"Method","_domains":["world_model"],"_tasks":[],"venue":"Nature Communications","venue_tier":"T1","citation_count":0},{"id":"openalex:W7220743086","title":"Large-scale metagenomic characterization of the vaginal microbiome and uropathogens in women with recent bacterial vaginosis and urinary tract infections","authors":["Sonia N. Whang","Xinyue Wang","Krystal J. Thomas-White","Genevieve Olmschenk","John E. Garza","Pita Navarro","Nicole M. Gilbert"],"published":